msgstr ":py:obj:`Translation <hlib.maths.translation.Translation>`\\"

msgid "class hlib.maths.vector.Vector"
msgstr "class hlib.maths.vector.Vector"

msgid "ベースクラス: :py:obj:`maya.api.OpenMaya.MVector`"
msgstr "Base class: :py:obj:`maya.api.OpenMaya.MVector`"

msgid "om2.MVector を継承した3成分の可変なベクトル値。"
msgstr "A 3-component, variable vector value that inherits from om2.MVector."

msgid "``om2.MVector`` の派生クラスなので、hlib の Vector をそのまま OpenMaya API 2.0 の 関数・コンストラクタへ渡せる。コンストラクタは ``Vector()`` (ゼロ)、 ``Vector(x, y, z)``、``Vector(x, y)`` (z=0)、``Vector([x, y, z])``、 ``Vector(MVector | MPoint)`` など om2 と同じ形を受け付け、加えて ``Vector(x=1, y=2, z=3)`` のキーワード引数(省略した成分は 0)も使える。 成分は数値だけで、文字列などの不正な引数は om2 と同じく ValueError になる。"
msgstr "Since it is a subclass of ``om2.MVector``, the hlib Vector can be passed directly to OpenMaya API 2.0 functions and constructors. The constructors accept the same forms as om2, such as ``Vector()`` (zero), ``Vector(x, y, z)``, ``Vector(x, y)`` (z=0), ``Vector([x, y, z])``, ``Vector(MVector | MPoint)``, etc., and additionally support keyword arguments like ``Vector(x=1, y=2, z=3)`` (missing components default to 0). Each component must be a number; invalid arguments such as strings will raise ValueError just like in om2."

msgid "演算子は om2 の意味論に従い、ベクトルの結果を基底の :class:`Vector` として返す (Translation などの派生型は保持しない)。``om2.MVector`` が左辺の ``+`` / ``-`` / ``^`` も、右辺の Vector の反射演算子が先に呼ばれるため Vector を返す。"
msgstr "Operators follow om2 semantics and return the vector result as the base :class:`Vector` (derived types such as Translation are not preserved). ``om2.MVector`` also returns a Vector for the left-hand side ``+`` / ``-`` / ``^``, because the reflection operator of the right-hand side Vector is called first, thus returning a Vector."

msgid "``+`` / ``-``: MVector 系同士の成分ごとの加減算。"
msgstr "``+`` / ``-``: Component-wise addition and subtraction of MVector-type objects."

msgid "``v * 数値`` / ``数値 * v`` / ``v / 数値``: スカラー倍。0 での除算は Maya のバージョンにかかわらず ZeroDivisionError。"
msgstr "``v * 数値`` / ``数値 * v`` / ``v / 数値``: Scalar multiplication. Division by zero will raise a ZeroDivisionError regardless of the Maya version."

msgid "``v * w``: 内積(float)。``v ^ w``: 外積。"
msgstr "``v * w``: Dot product (float). ``v ^ w``: Cross product."

msgid "``v * m`` (m は MMatrix 系): 行ベクトル規約の方向変換(平行移動を含まない)。"
msgstr "``v * m`` (where m is a MMatrix type): Direction conversion using row vector convention (without translation)."

msgid "``m * v``: om2 と同じく列ベクトルとしての積(``v * mᵀ`` と同じ)。"
msgstr "``m * v``: Like om2, the product is a column vector (same as ``v * mᵀ``)."

msgid "``+=`` / ``-=`` / ``*=`` / ``/=`` / ``^=`` は自身を書き換えて派生型を保つ (``v *= w`` だけは om2 と同じく内積の float へ名前を束ね直す)。値は可変で ``x``/``y``/``z`` や添字へ代入でき、ハッシュは不可(dict のキーや set には 使えない)。添字は -3〜2 の整数で、範囲外は IndexError。スライスは成分の tuple を 返す(代入には使えない)。"
msgstr "``+=`` / ``-=`` / ``*=`` / ``/=`` / ``^=`` modify themselves while preserving their type (except for ``v *= w``, which like om2 rebinds to a float for dot products). Values are mutable and can be assigned to via ``x``/``y``/``z`` or indexing, but they cannot be used as dictionary keys or in sets. Indices must be integers from -3 to 2; out-of-range indices raise IndexError. Slicing returns a tuple of components (slicing assignment is not supported)."

msgid "``==`` は om2 と同じ成分の完全一致で、MVector 系であれば派生型が異なっても 等しくなり得る。MVector 系以外との比較は例外にしない(om2 の型なら False、 それ以外は相手の比較に委ね、どちらも判断しなければ False)。ただし om2 の型が 左辺の比較(``om2.MPoint() == Vector()`` など)は om2 側が TypeError を送出する。"
msgstr "``==`` is strictly equal only if the components are identical to those in om2. For MVector and related types, even if the derived types differ, they can still be equal. Comparisons with non-MVector types are not exceptions (if either type is from om2, return False; otherwise, delegate to the other's comparison logic, returning False if neither can determine the result). However, when an om2 type is on the left side of a comparison (such as ``om2.MPoint() == Vector()``), the om2 side will raise a TypeError."

msgid "数学値を返す継承メソッドも対応するhlib型を返す。OpenMayaの演算と 自身の更新有無を維持する。クラス定数はOpenMayaの共有値なので変更しない。"
msgstr "Inherited methods returning math values also return the corresponding hlib types. OpenMaya calculations and mutation behavior are preserved. Class constants are shared OpenMaya values and must not be modified."

